closer-automation-isolation + permanent per-lead stop-word block (2026-07-16).

Covers:
  1. Exact stop-word matching (_is_post_followup_disable_word, active def).
  2. Durable per-lead automation-stop state (lead_auto_state additive
     columns + _set_lead_automation_stopped: idempotent, never auto-cleared,
     survives "restart" i.e. reopening the same sqlite file).
  3. Ordinary-manager automation before/after the stop word (_lead_automation_gate).
  4. Closer isolation (day/night toggle default OFF, enabled-but-empty-text
     fails closed, every non-greeting kind denied unconditionally).
  5. Combined rules (stop word beats an enabled closer toggle; other
     lead/manager unaffected).
  6. Role preservation (storage.manager_add's new optional role= param).
  7. ManagerBot UI (new closer day/night greeting toggle buttons).
  8. Security/static (gate wired into every real send path, no AdminBot/
     PartnerBot changes, allow_spend count unchanged, production-path DB guard).

Techniques: main.py/manager_bot.py cannot be imported standalone (Telethon/
env side effects at import time) -- functions under test are extracted via
ast.parse + ast.unparse + exec(), the same technique used throughout
tools/*_selftest.py (see tools/closer_settings_selftest.py). storage.py IS
directly importable (used elsewhere the same way, e.g.
tools/manager_replacement_backend_selftest.py) so Section 6 imports it for
real. All DB access is against temporary sqlite files created by this
script; a _selftest_db_guard refuses any path under <repo>/db. No Telegram,
no network, no real proxy/API calls.

    python3.12 tools\\closer_stopword_gate_selftest.py
